      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Let $A=Z,$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation.",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}$ such that $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\,|\\,(x+y)}\n$$",
